# Conda environment `hispec`

When running **pytest**, **Python one-offs** (e.g. preview or CCF smoke tests), or any command that imports `hispecdrp` for verification in this repository, use the **`hispec`** conda environment so NumPy/Numba and other pins match the project.

Preferred patterns (pick one):

- `conda run -n hispec pytest …`
- `conda run -n hispec python …`
- Or activate first: `conda activate hispec` then run `pytest` / `python` in the same shell session.

Do not assume the default shell Python is compatible (e.g. avoid ad-hoc `python` / `pytest` without the env when validating this codebase).
